{BOX()}
!! cmavo: bai (BAI)

!!! Proposed Definition

Compelled by... Tags a sumti as fitting the 1st place of bapli. Augments the bridi in which it occurs, adding an extra place with the meaning of the 1st place of bapli and then fills it with the tagged sumti. In other words, the event described by the bridi is compelled by the referent of the tagged sumti.

!!! Proposed Tag
bapli modal

!!! See Also
* {bapli)
* {se bai}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* Compelled by...

!!! Usage Examples
''.i za'a bai lo skami mi nalviska le se cinri nu casnu'' (Rather modified.)%%%
Apparently, the computer compels me to not see the interesting discussion.
{BOX}
{BOX()}
!! cmavo: se bai (BAI*)
!! Proposed Definition

Forcing result... Tags a sumti as fitting the 2nd place of bapli. Augments the bridi in which it occurs, adding an extra place with the meaning of the 2nd place of bapli and then fills it with the tagged sumti. In other words, the event described by the bridi compels the result described by the referent of the tagged sumti.

!!! Proposed Tag
se bapli modal

!!! See Also
* {bapli}
* {bai}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* Forcing result

!!! Usage Examples
Artificial:
''mi darxi le bolci se bai lo nu ri gunro farlu fi le gapru traji mokca be le cmalu cmana''%%%
I hit the ball forcing it to roll down from the top of the hill.
{BOX}
{BOX()}
!! cmavo: fau (BAI)

!!! Proposed Definition

In the event of... Tags a sumti as fitting the 1st place of fasnu. Augments the bridi in which it occurs, adding an extra place with the meaning of the 1st place of fasnu and then fills it with the tagged sumti. In other words, the event described by the bridi is associated with an event described by referent of the tagged sumti. 

!!! Proposed Tag
fasnu modal

!!! See Also
* {fasnu}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* In the event of...

!!! Usage Examples
Artificial:
''.i fau le nu mi sanli binxo kei mi cusku le se du'u mo'u citka''%%%
With the event of standing up, I express that the eating is over.
{BOX}
{BOX()}
!! cmavo: sau (BAI)

!!! Proposed definition

Requiring... Tags a sumti as fitting the 1st place of sarcu. Augments the bridi in which it occurs, adding an extra place with the meaning of the 1st place of sarcu and then fills it with the tagged sumti. In other words, the event described by the bridi requires the referent of the tagged sumti.

!!! Proposed Tag
sarcu modal

!!! See Also
* {sarcu}
* {se sau}
* {te sau}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* Requiring...

!!! Usage Examples
Artificial:
''.i do nenri sau tu'a le ckiku valsi''%%%
You enter, with requirement the key word.
{BOX}
{BOX()}
!! cmavo: se sau (BAI*)

!!! Proposed Definition

Required for... Tags a sumti as fitting the 2nd place of sarcu. Augments the bridi in which it occurs, adding an extra place with the meaning of the 2nd place of sarcu and then fills it with the tagged sumti. In other words, the event described by the bridi is required for the referent of the tagged sumti.

!!! Proposed Tag
se sarcu modal

!!! See Also
* {sarcu}
* {sau}
* {te sau}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* Required for...

!!! Usage Examples
''.i .e'o ko sanli vi le serti se sau le nu mi fi do badgau'' (Slightly modified.)%%%
Please stand at the stairs, which is required for my defending you.
{BOX}
{BOX()}
!! cmavo: te sau (BAI*)

!!! Proposed Definition

Required under conditions... Tags a sumti as fitting the 3rd place of sarcu. Augments the bridi in which it occurs, adding an extra place with the meaning of the 3rd place of sarcu and then fills it with the tagged sumti. In other words, the event described by the bridi is required under the conditions described by the referent of the tagged sumti.

!!! Proposed Tag
te sarcu modal

!!! See Also
* {sarcu}
* {sau}
* {se sau}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* Required under conditions...

!!! Usage Examples
Artificial:
''mi klama le briju te sau lo nu mi gunka''%%%
I go to the office as required by my work.
{BOX}
{BOX()}
!! cmavo: ja'e (BAI)

!!! Proposed Definition

Therefore result... Tags a sumti as fitting the 1st place of jalge. Augments the bridi in which it occurs, adding an extra place with the meaning of the 1st place of jalge and then fills it with the tagged sumti. In other words, the event described by the bridi results from the tagged sumti.

!!! Proposed Tag
jalge modal

!!! See Also
* {jalge}
* {se ja'e}
* {ja'e nai}
* {se ja'e nai}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* Therefore result...

!!! Usage Examples
''.i le li'i clupa nu casnu bau roda ja'e node cu rinka'' (Slightly modified.)%%%
The experience of a looping discussion in all languages which results in nothing is the cause.
{BOX}
{BOX()}
!! cmavo: ja'e nai (BAI*)

!!! Proposed Definition

Without result... Tags a sumti as not fitting the 1st place of jalge. Augments the bridi in which it occurs, adding an extra place with the meaning of the 1st place of jalge and then fills it with the tagged sumti.  In other words, the event described by the bridi does not result in the referent of the tagged sumti.

!!! Proposed Tag
na'e jalge modal

!!! Proposed Keywords
* Without result...

!!! Usage Examples
''.i ja'e nai bo mi na ka'e sipna''%%%
Regardless of this, I am not able to sleep.
{BOX}
{BOX()}
!! cmavo: se ja'e (BAI*)

!!! Proposed Definition

Results because ... Tags a sumti as fitting the 2nd place of jalge. Augments the bridi in which it occurs, adding an extra place with the meaning of the 2nd place of jalge and then fills it with the tagged sumti. In other words, the event described by the bridi results because of the referent of the tagged sumti.

!!! Proposed Tag
se jalge modal

!!! See Also
* {jalge}
* {ja'e}
* {ja'e nai}
* {se ja'e nai}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* Results because...

!!! Usage Examples
Artificial:
''mi cadzu se ja'e lo nu mi na ponse lo karce''%%%
I walk because I don't own a car.
{BOX}
{BOX()}
!! cmavo: se ja'e nai (BAI*)

!!! Proposed Definition

Results not because... Tags a sumti as not fitting the 2nd place of jalge. Augments the bridi in which it occurs, adding an extra place with the meaning of the 2nd place of jalge and then fills it with the tagged sumti.  In other words, the event described by the bridi is not the reason for the referent of the tagged sumti.

!!! Proposed Tag
na'e se jalge modal

!!! See Also
* {jalge}
* {ja'e}
* {se ja'e}
* {ja'e nai}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* Results not because...

!!! Usage Examples
Artificial:
''mi cadzu se ja'e nai lo nu mi na ponse lo karce''%%%
I walk, but not because I don't own a car.%%%
I walk regardless of whether or not I own a car.
{BOX}
{BOX()}
!! cmavo: va'o (BAI)

!!! Proposed Definition

Under conditions... Tags a sumti as fitting the 1st place of vanbi. Augments the bridi in which it occurs, adding an extra place with the meaning of the 1st place of vanbi and then fills it with the tagged sumti. In other words, the event described by the bridi occurs under the conditions described by the tagged sumti.  See also: vanbi, se va'o.

!!! Proposed Tag
vanbi modal

!!! See Also
* {vanbi}
* {se va'o}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* Under conditions...

!!! Usage Examples
''.i .e'o ko na damba va'o le nu rodo na kakne le nu damba bau la lojban.''%%%
Under the conditions of y'all not being able to fight in lojban, please don't fight.
{BOX}
{BOX()}
!! cmavo: se va'o (BAI*)

!!! Proposed Definition

As conditions for... Tags a sumti as fitting the 2nd place of vanbi. Augments the bridi in which it occurs, adding an extra place with the meaning of the 2nd place of vanbi and then fills it with the tagged sumti. In other words, the event described by the bridi is the condition under which the referent of the tagged sumti occurs.

!!! Proposed Tag
se vanbi modal

!!! See Also
* {vanbi}
* {va'o}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* As conditions for...

!!! Usage Examples
Artificial:
''la .bais. cu mulno se va'o lo nu la camgusmis cu gleki''%%%
The BAI sections are complete as a condition for Robin (camgusmis) being happy.
{BOX}
! Notes

! Impact

There exists a contradiction between the CLL and the ma'oste about the meaning of BAInai WRT causals. The interpretation we are using (explicated in the preface section) here for "ri'a nai" and such matches with that found in the CLL (Chapter 9, Section 13). To get the meaning shown in the ma'oste (despite...), it is suggested to use e.g. to'eri'anai instead of ri'anai.

This is shown as the following:

* ri'a == with cause
* ri'anai == not with cause (regardless of cause)
* to'eri'a == prevented by 
* to'eri'anai == not prevented by (despite)

! Poll

{POLL(pollId=>17)}BPFK Poll: Causation sumtcita{POLL}
